    "### What “expand seeds into a network” actually means\n",
    "\n",
    "Imagine two biologically annotated genes with no direct edge, `TF_A` and `TF_D`, connected through `TF_B` and `TF_C`. Restricting the network to the annotated genes alone would lose the actual signaling path. This stage therefore brings in **one-hop regulators and targets**, optionally keeps **short connecting paths** irrespective of direction during path search, and adds nearby genes that display **known activity changes** along the differentiation tree. The retained SIF preserves every original edge direction and sign.\n",
    "\n",
    "The cap does **not** indiscriminately truncate the important anchors: `mandatory = seeds ∪ bridge_nodes ∪ extra_dynamic`, and the code raises an error if this mandatory set already exceeds the cap. Remaining slots are assigned to connected genes, then weakly connected components that contain no seed are discarded. **No SCC extraction happens yet.**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "8f452bd6",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7. Expand MSigDB seeds into a reduced DoRothEA network\n",
    "\n",
    "The selected seeds are now **automatically taken from the downloaded MSigDB**, rather than hard-coded. Include 1-hop upstream and downstream regulatory neighbors, optionally preserve short bridges and additional switching genes. Do not prefilter to the largest SCC: upstream genes outside an SCC may still matter. This network becomes the **candidate input** to BoNesis, not the final optimized selection.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Important:** `MAX_CANDIDATE_GENES` is a resource guard. If the mandatory seeds, bridges, and dynamic additions exceed it, the notebook raises an explicit error rather than silently dropping seeds. Reduce `SEED_TOP_N`, `N_EXTRA_DYNAMIC`, or increase the cap.\n"
   ]
  },
